Package: picphotoviewer
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Neils Karlson <nktrabajo@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, python3-pyside6.qtprintsupport, python3-pil, exiftran, libglib2.0-bin, pkexec, xdg-utils
Recommends: qt6-image-formats-plugins, python3-nautilus, libnotify-bin, xclip
Homepage: https://github.com/nktrabajo/Pic-Photo-Viewer
Description: photo viewer that opens over the desktop, Picasa style
 PicPhotoViewer shows a photo over a translucent layer on top of the desktop,
 with a filmstrip of the folder and a toolbar: zoom, slideshow, lossless
 rotation, stars compatible with .picasa.ini, print, copy and trash.
 .
 From the viewer or from the Nautilus context menu it can set a photo as the
 desktop background on one, several or all monitors (with a diagram of the
 real monitor layout), and as the GDM login screen background.
